# fem-em-solver scheduled automation — see docs/automation/ in the repo.
#
# FULL SCHEDULE, restored 2026-09-28 (operator directive; ends the 2026-09-13
# wind-down now that Opus 5.5 carries the implementer and daily-review load).
#   - Three daily reviews (Opus 5.5 via review-model.env, 45 min cap) at
#     03:00 / 10:30 / 18:00, every day. Each is followed by a four-slot
#     interval; the §9 restock floor is 160 MEASURED slot-minutes per
#     four-slot interval (2026-10-01; was 240 predicted).
#   - Twelve Opus implementer runs (65 min hard kill) per day, every day:
#     00:00, 04:30, 06:00, 07:30, 09:00, 12:00, 13:30, 15:00, 16:30, 19:30,
#     21:00, 22:30 — except that 21:00 is dropped on Monday, Wednesday and
#     Saturday, when the weekly holds that window (11 slots on those days).
#   - Three weekly planning reviews (Fable 5.1, high effort, 60 min cap),
#     Monday, Wednesday and Saturday 21:00 (Monday added 2026-10-02, operator
#     directive: gaps 48 / 48 / 72 h instead of 72 / 96; the dailies may also
#     extend live chains provisionally, §9 rule (6)). Twelve slots a day drain
#     one weekly's chain list in about two days. 21:00
#     rather than the pre-wind-down 02:15: on 09-06 and 09-13 the 02:15 run
#     exhausted the account's 5-hour allowance and took the 03:00 review and
#     two slots with it. A weekly ends by 22:02, before the 22:30 slot.
#   - XL / XXL windows and housekeeping are UNCHANGED: cron scripts with no
#     Claude session, zero tokens.
# Sessions never overlap; all Claude runs share one flock (a collision makes
# the later run skip, never wait). Per-command compute stays under the repo's
# tier ceilings. Wind-down grid (2026-09-13 .. 09-28): git history.
0 3 * * * /home/user/fem-em-solver/scripts/automation/daily-review.sh
30 10 * * * /home/user/fem-em-solver/scripts/automation/daily-review.sh
0 18 * * * /home/user/fem-em-solver/scripts/automation/daily-review.sh
30 4,7,13,16,19,22 * * * /home/user/fem-em-solver/scripts/automation/implementer-run.sh
0 0,6,9,12,15 * * * /home/user/fem-em-solver/scripts/automation/implementer-run.sh
0 21 * * 0,2,4,5 /home/user/fem-em-solver/scripts/automation/implementer-run.sh
0 21 * * 1,3,6 /home/user/fem-em-solver/scripts/automation/weekly-review.sh
# Sunday 01:45: mechanical log-retention sweep (no Claude session; ~1 min).
# See docs/testing/retention-policy.md §4.
45 1 * * 0 /home/user/fem-em-solver/scripts/automation/housekeeping.sh
# 02:00 Sun-Fri: the XL window (4 h, 512 GiB — 2026-09-13; was 2 h), if one is queued in
# docs/testing/xl-queue.env (operator directive 2026-09-09). No Claude
# session — a cron script has neither the 660 s foreground cap nor the 65-min
# slot kill. 02:00 because the box is shared with work this sandbox cannot
# see. Own lock, not the automation flock. Budget six per trailing 7 days (2026-09-13),
# enforced by the guard against xl-ledger.md; fires nightly and does nothing
# once the budget is spent or the queue is empty. Worst case ends 06:00, so a
# full window overlaps the 04:30 implementer slot (and the 06:00 one at its
# kill): 16 XL ranks plus a 2-8 rank slot job on the 36-core box, accepted by
# the operator 2026-09-13 as the price of the longer window; the XL job holds
# its own lock, not the automation flock, so neither waits for the other.
0 2 * * 0-5 /home/user/fem-em-solver/scripts/automation/xl-run.sh xl
# 02:00 Saturday: the XXL window (8 h, 754 GiB, one per week), from
# docs/testing/xxl-queue.env. Its own day so the two tiers never both
# start at 02:00; 8 h from 02:00 ends at 10:00 and overlaps the 04:30-09:00
# slots (2-8 rank jobs on a 36-core box — the one deliberately oversubscribed
# window). Operator directive 2026-09-10.
0 2 * * 6 /home/user/fem-em-solver/scripts/automation/xl-run.sh xxl
#
# CANONICAL COPY. The live schedule lives in the user crontab spool; this file
# is the version-controlled source of truth for it. Install with:
#     crontab scripts/automation/crontab
# Verify with `crontab -l`. Scheduled sessions cannot install it themselves:
# /var/spool/cron is outside the sandbox's write scope and only `crontab -l`
# is in .claude/settings.json's excludedCommands, so a change here reaches
# cron only when a human (or an unsandboxed session) runs the install.
